<title>USA: Hyatt to spend $1 billion on acquisitions - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Hyatt to spend $1 billion on acquisitions - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Closely held Hyatt Hotels Corp plans to spend as much as $1 billion during the coming three years to acquire 20 to 30 hotels, the Wall Street Journal said Monday.</p>
<p>Hyatt officials told the paper the company is seeking upscale hotels and resorts in the United States, and possibly in Canada and the Caribbean.</p>
<p>The report said Hyatt plans to announce the plan today. The acquisitions would be done through a newly formed entity, Hyatt Equities LLC, the report said.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
